  &= \frac{1}{6} + \frac{1}{6} - \frac{2 \,(1 \,(1/6)) \,(1/6)}{6} \\
  &= \frac{11}{36}
\end{align*}

The probability that the remaining five dice show other numbers than 1 or 2 is:

\begin{equation}
P(Dice\neq 1, Dice\neq 2) = (1-\frac{1}{6})^5 = \frac{5}{6^5}
